+# other voice buffer in the same table is 0x900. The heap walks its free list, finds nothing
+# that large and correctly returns null, and the game stores that null without checking it.
+# Clamping the request to 0x7fff, which the allocator rounds to 32KB, is enough: the only
+# copy ever observed into that buffer is 0x7ff8 bytes at offset 4.
