+# GRAND THEFT AUTO IV, BLUS30682 v01.02 (Complete Edition) and the same executable sold as
+# BLUS30127 / NPUB30702 v01.08 -- ours. With SPU XFloat Accuracy on Approximate, Niko falls
+# through floors, roads and cars; RPCS3's database pins the game to Accurate for that, which
+# costs a lot of SPU time. With this patch on, ConfigDatabase.LOCAL_OVERRIDES puts these three
+# serials back on Approximate.
+#
+# The collision job SpuCollide_psn_final.task.elf starts its searches with "max distance"
+# set to 0x7FFFFFFF, the SPU's largest float (~6.8e38; the SPU has no NaN or infinity). On
+# Approximate that bit pattern is a NaN, so the search's first "still converging?" test,
+# (prev - dist) > prev * 1e-6 with prev = max (LS 0xea28..0xea54), comes out false and it
+# stops before it finds the ground. 0x7F7FFFFF (FLT_MAX) gives every test in the job the
+# same answer and is a number on both. All 14 places build the value with ilhu 0x7fff +
+# iohl 0xffff; this changes the ilhu half. None is a bit mask: every AND they meet is with
+# the xyz mask at LS 0x1d890. numeric_limits<float>::max() in .data (LS 0x1dc18) must NOT be
+# changed: lowest() is compared bit for bit against 0xffffffff "unset" fill.
+#
+# Harmless on Accurate, where both values are finite. On the Complete Edition the two
+# Episodes from Liberty City run inside this same executable as add-on content (ELC/DLC1,
+# ELC/DLC2): a Ballad of Gay Tony boot loaded the same SpuCollide and took all 14 lines. The
+# standalone Episodes from Liberty City disc is a different executable and is not covered.
+#
+# Offsets are LS addresses: apply_modification subtracts p_vaddr (0x3000).
+# Ps3PatchRepo.BUNDLED must list this, or it is imported but never enabled.
+SPU-d0a1508208613e2184fbd64906d34d5f07890033:
+  "ARMSX3 Approximate collision fix":
