+# BATMAN: ARKHAM ORIGINS, US releases (BLUS31147, BLUS31207, NPUB31261) update 01.06, multiplayer executable
+# (MP.SELF) -- ours, OFF by default. The US releases run the same MP.SELF.
+#
+# Online play on Arkham: Revived meets only RPCN players, and a private lobby's host gets no START GAME
+# button until 3 players are in. The lobby script (BmScript GDGFxMovieUI_LobbyMenu, cooked into the
+# disc's MULTIPLAYER/BMGAME/COOKEDPS3/FRONTEND.XXX) decides it with
+#     IsReadyToStartPrivateGame(NumPlayers) = NumPlayers >= (class'GDWorldInfo'.static.IsShippingBuild() ? 3 : 1)
+# and PopulateLobbyListTeam only asks after bIsLobbyHost, so only the host needs this patch: players
+# with and without it can share a lobby. Public lobbies (start once full) are left alone.
+#
+# IsShippingBuild() cannot simply return false: RGameInfo.AllowCheats is "return !IsShippingBuild()",
+# so that would allow cheats online. Nor can 0xcfe50, the li r3,1 it calls: that function is shared by
+# 29 callers. The cave replaces that call inside AWorldInfo::execIsShippingBuild (0xf76ec4) and answers
+# "not shipping" only when the script bytes right after the call are the private check's own
+# "? 3 : 1": 00 02 7c 03 00 01 0f 5e (skip 2, byte 3, skip 1, one, end of parms; Arkham Origins
+# shuffles the bytecode token values). There r4 is the script frame and r5 its code pointer, already
+# past the call (P_FINISH). Every other caller still gets "shipping", and the private minimum becomes
+# 1, the developers' own rule.
+#
+# Deliberately NOT in Ps3PatchRepo.BUNDLED: it changes a game rule rather than fixing a broken game,
+# so it stays off until the host turns it on.
